mode prove
triangle A B C
perp_bisector p B C

# First stress-run pattern.
foot M B p
reflection_point T C B
reflection_point P T M
parallel qC C p
reflection_line R1 A qC
prove_concyclic A B P R1

# Second stress-run pattern.
reflection_point D A B
foot F D qC
parallel qB B p
foot G A qB
reflection_point E A C
reflection_line R2 E p
prove_concyclic A F G R2

# The orthogonal-component theorem proves A,F,G,R2 cyclic.  That new cyclic
# fact must feed the circumcenter radius-completion rule on the next closure
# pass, rather than stopping after a single sweep.
circumcenter O A F G
prove_equal_distance O A O R2
